      {
        "value": "The California Grey was developed in California in the 1930s by James Dryden to be a dual-purpose hen that stayed productive longer than two years. Its Barred Rock x White Leghorn cross gave it naturally autosexed grey barred plumage, but it never gained commercial popularity and is now rare.",
